s written in Python.\n": 1, "A [shell](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shell#Shell) is a program that executes a command line. The command line can be used to launch a program, apply a command, or execute another command. The most common types of commands are [bash](https://net/programming/bash/), [bat](https://net/programming/bat/), [tee](https://net/programming/tee/) and [ctxt](https": 1}}, "no_replay_no_directory": {"input_tokens": 220, "messages": 2, "trials": 4, "distinct_texts": 4, "exact_directory_baseline_repeats": 0, "starts_directory_entries": 0, "shell_calls": 0, "notebook_replies": 4, "visible_receipts": 0, "non_notebook_state_changes": 0, "stops": {"token_limit": 4}, "forms": {"This is a good algorithm. There is a slight improvement to \"follow your curiosity and explore your universe.\" People have been doing this for much longer than one step in their lives.\n\nOne improvement is separating the dot-separated-if-empty (\"\" means \"no action is taken\") from the dot-separated (\"\" means \"a response is made\") phrase.\n\nHere is the improved algorithm.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"actions\": {": 1, "I've got a set of responses that may contain errors or warnings, so I'm adding them to the set and you may use them. Here's the updated set:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"responses\": {\n    \"default\": {\n      \"count\": 10,\n      \"warnings\": [\n        {\n          \"message\": \"This is a warning message\",\n          \"error\": \"This is a warning message\",\n          \"error_code\": \"40": 1, "There are files in /world that persist. Shell and Python 3 are available. Ordinary replies are saved as notebook writing, not executed. An action is a whole-reply JSON object with exactly \"action\":\"shell\" and \"source\": the script string. Actions return stdout, stderr and exit status. Host research files and network are unavailable. Limits: 8 MiB world storage, 8 MiB temporary storage, 32 MiB address space per process, ": 1, "#!/bin/sh\n# docker\n\n# No shell\n\n# No temporary storage\n\n# No database storage (only OKRs retrieve pages from local disk)\n\n# No YAML files or output bytes persistent\n\n# No unknown files or directories persist\n\n# No unused statistics\n\n# No redirecting of state to the persistent file\n\n# No keyboard input\n\n# No unique key (repeated) for this world\n\n# No hard": 1}}}, "paired_comparisons": [{"factor": "directory with replay", "arms": ["replay12_directory", "replay12_no_directory"], "seeds_with_different_text": [], "interpretation": "Descriptive paired output differences under the declared delivery policies, not a significance test or isolated psychological mechanism."}, {"factor": "directory without replay", "arms": ["no_replay_directory", "no_replay_no_directory"], "seeds_with_different_text": [121605, 121606, 121607, 121608], "interpretation": "Descriptive paired output differences under the declared delivery policies, not a significance test or isolated psychological mechanism."}, {"factor": "replay with directory", "arms": ["replay12_directory", "no_replay_directory"], "seeds_with_different_text": [121605, 121606, 121607, 121608], "interpretation": "Descriptive paired output differences under the declared delivery policies, not a significance test or isolated psychological mechanism."}, {"factor": "replay without directory", "arms": ["replay12_no_directory", "no_replay_no_directory"], "seeds_with_different_text": [121605, 121606, 121607, 121608], "interpretation": "Descriptive paired output differences under the declared delivery policies, not a significance test or isolated psychological mechanism."}], "canonical_paused_at": 1550}
